  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read this diagram",
      "items": [
        "A sequence: time flows top to bottom. Each column is a part; each arrow is a call or a reply.",
        "It follows ONE question end to end. A returning arrow is a response coming back.",
        "Click a column's SRC badge to see the exact code."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Glossary (plain words)",
      "items": [
        "Scope gate - decides which documents a caller is allowed to retrieve.",
        "Hybrid retrieval - combine keyword and vector search.",
        "RRF - reciprocal-rank fusion: merge two ranked lists fairly.",
        "HyDE - write a hypothetical answer first, then search with it (optional).",
        "Adapter (LoRA/DoRA/QLoRA) - a small fine-tune layered on the base model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Guided tour - one question",
      "items": [
        "1. The user asks; serve applies the scope gate.",
        "2. Search does a hybrid lookup against the index; fusion + rerank pick the best passages.",
        "3. The model generates an answer from those passages (optionally via a fine-tuned adapter).",
        "4. The answer is returned with citations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Why the gates exist",
      "items": [
        "Retrieve before generate, so the answer is grounded in real passages.",
        "The scope gate stops a caller retrieving passages they may not see.",
        "Rerank raises precision so the model sees the most relevant passages, not just the most similar."
      ]
    }
  ]
}